From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kant <283011337+muradkant@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 19:53:33 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] pipewire: record only the requested node, robustly

- Never fall back to another device. A source that does not exist was
  replaced by the default one, and routing policy could later move or
  restore the stream onto anything else; either way the recording got
  sound nobody chose. Resolve the node once, target it by serial, and
  opt out of fallback, moving, reconnection and remembered state.
- Accept a sink's PulseAudio monitor name (X.monitor) for the sink X.
- Honour the chunk offset and clamp the chunk to its buffer; carry
  partial codec frames over without a fixed-size, overflowable buffer.
- Date the first captured sample rather than the cycle that delivered
  it, publish it atomically to the encoder thread, and request a
  quantum of one codec frame.
- Stop with an error when the stream fails or the source stops
  delivering samples for 3 seconds, instead of recording on without
  sound.
---
 src/pipewire.cpp | 209 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------------
 src/pipewire.hpp |  26 ++++--
 2 files changed, 174 insertions(+), 61 deletions(-)

